<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bukkur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bhakkar Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bukkur is a limestone island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> river between the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkur">Sukkur</a> and Rohri in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, crowned by an old fortress. Called Bhakkar in Persian chronicles, it commanded the river crossing and was a key stronghold of the Arghun dynasty and later of Mughal governors of upper Sindh. The fort is now largely ruined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bukkur.jpg" alt="Bukkur" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Facebook · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vintage_picture_of_Bhakkar_Fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
